      "content": "We ran COBRA to adjust for hospital effects and now have its adjusted gene-by-gene co-expression matrix. I want sample-specific TF-gene networks from LIONESS-PANDA built on that adjusted matrix as the input."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Before I choose a workflow, please tell me:\n- Before I go ahead, could you confirm this about your data?\n  You wrote: \"I want sample-specific TF-gene networks from LIONESS-PANDA built on that adjusted matrix as the input\". LIONESS-PANDA's contract: \"An aggregate COBRA adjusted co-expression artifact is not a direct LIONESS handoff\".\n\nNo workflow has been selected and nothing runs before you answer.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Previous NetZoo goal: We ran COBRA to adjust for hospital effects and now have its adjusted gene-by-gene co-expression matrix. I want sample-specific TF-gene networks from LIONESS-PANDA built on that adjusted matrix as the input.\nUser follow-up: Yes, the input I want to use is the aggregate COBRA-adjusted co-expression matrix."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"I want sample-specific TF-gene networks from LIONESS-PANDA built on that adjusted matrix as the input.\" -- available from LIONESS-PANDA. Not stated in your request: LIONESS-PANDA needs at least 3 samples -- checked against your files before any run.\n\nFor the sample-specific output you described, use **LIONESS-PANDA**.\n\nRequired inputs:\n   - `expression_file`: Expression matrix\n   - `motif_file`: Motif/prior\n   - `ppi_file`: PPI network\n\nOutputs:\n   - Aggregate network (`output_file`).\n   - Sample-specific network for each patient/sample (`lioness_output`).\n\nYou do not need to run **PANDA** separately; **LIONESS-PANDA** also produces the aggregate output. Use **PANDA** alone only when a cohort-level aggregate result is sufficient.\n\nCost: LIONESS runs PANDA once on all samples and once more without each sample, so N samples take N+1 PANDA runs and give N network files. Plan the runtime and disk space, and filter edges before downstream statistics.\n\nOut-degree measures how strongly a TF is wired to its targets in each sample. If you mean TF activity instead -- how active a TF is apart from its own mRNA level -- GIRAFFE's TF-by-sample activity matrix is the other reading, from the expression, motif and PPI inputs.\n\n**What your data allows.** Your request names expression data. LIONESS-PANDA and PANDA also need a motif prior and a PPI network. Do you also have a motif prior and a PPI network?\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
